WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:05.190
Next, we're going to take a look at some of the settings you can update that will affect

2
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.570
the handling of your vehicle.

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.009
We'll look at what happens when you tweak the value of the center of mass inside the

4
00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:15.509
vehicle blueprint, and then how we can tweak some of the settings inside the wheel blueprints

5
00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:20.179
themselves to fine-tune the cornering of the vehicle.

6
00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:25.059
So to tweak the center of mass, if you open up your vehicle blueprint and select

7
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:33.969
the vehicle movement component, just kind of search for center of mass here, and we'll

8
00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:38.670
enable the center of mass override so that we can set some manual values.

9
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.149
And you know, you can move the center of mass forwards and backwards, up and down,

10
00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:46.119
left or right, depending on what values you put in these axes.

11
00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:50.320
So to move it forwards and backwards, we could do that with the X axis here.

12
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:59.310
So let's say we move it backwards 50 units and see how that affects our vehicle's handling.

13
00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:04.269
So you can see as I turn now when we've got some sort of speed up with our acceleration,

14
00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:09.269
the back end flies out because a lot of the mass is no longer over the center of

15
00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.269
the vehicle.

16
00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:13.569
It's quite far back.

17
00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:18.329
And we can come back here and tweak those values and do the same for Y, for example.

18
00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:24.219
So let's say 100 in Y and put it right the way off to the side.

19
00:01:24.219 --> 00:01:29.680
You can see that already that's quite a detrimental effect on our vehicle, but you could see

20
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:35.040
how that's quite a useful thing for maybe you wanted to update that runtime and change

21
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:41.390
the values on your vehicle, depending on what sort of scenario you're in.

22
00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:46.829
And if we were to update it in Z, for example, so if we go 200 units above the floor,

23
00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:52.430
this might be a bit too much, it's time to freak out a little bit, but you can see

24
00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.569
how that really makes your vehicle quite unstable.

25
00:01:55.569 --> 00:01:59.849
Also, you have to be fairly conservative with these depending on what kind of feeling you

26
00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:03.099
want to get out of your vehicle.

27
00:02:03.099 --> 00:02:08.099
Some other settings we can change are inside the wheel blueprints themselves.

28
00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:17.830
So if we just open both of those up, two things that we could tweak to adjust the

29
00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:22.629
sort of feeling of the handling are the cornering stiffness and the friction force

30
00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:24.479
multiplier.

31
00:02:24.479 --> 00:02:28.500
So with the rear wheels, for example, if we were to bring the cornering stiffness

32
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:38.370
down to a quarter of what it was, and then hit play, you'll see that that gives us the

33
00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:43.759
back end sliding out just a little bit, as we lose some of that friction and some of

34
00:02:43.759 --> 00:02:48.180
that grip that we had on it, we can see that immediately gives you quite a different

35
00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.659
feel to your vehicle, and allows you to kind of tweak it and get some get some cool

36
00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:56.439
feeling results quite quickly.

37
00:02:56.439 --> 00:03:01.620
If we were to do that with the front wheels as well, we could do something like, well,

38
00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:05.379
if we go, if we were to go the opposite direction, like increase the friction on

39
00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:15.300
both of these wheels, we put that back up to 1000, maybe this to four as well,

40
00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.300
you'll see that the vehicle sticks to the road quite well, and doesn't let the

41
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.569
back end or front end fly out at all.

42
00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:27.810
Even when we go at full speed, and I hit sort of A or D to turn left or right,

43
00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.129
we're sticking to the road really, really nicely.

44
00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:33.650
And that's just because we're increasing that friction, and we're increasing the

45
00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:40.120
stiffness for the cornering.

46
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.840
And inside both of these blueprints, there are lots and lots of different

47
00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.919
settings you can tweak here for adjusting how the vehicle feels.

48
00:03:46.919 --> 00:03:50.520
So you've got the obviously the wheels here that we've got access to stuff like

49
00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:55.120
friction and cornering stiffness, as well as suspension settings that are just how

50
00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:02.189
your the body of your car is reacting to the road that your vehicle is on,

51
00:04:02.189 --> 00:04:10.430
as well as inside the vehicle movement component of your vehicle's blueprint.

52
00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:17.459
So tweaking things like your engine, any sort of torque control setups and

53
00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:19.420
things like that you can do in here.

54
00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:23.579
So there is a lot of different options that you can kind of tweak and adjust to

55
00:04:23.579 --> 00:04:27.620
get your car feeling just how you want it to.

56
00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:31.819
But the general advice, but the general advice would be to just kind of

57
00:04:31.819 --> 00:04:35.740
tweak one thing at a time, and then test it out to see how that's affecting

58
00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.420
the handling of your vehicle.

59
00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.779
And slowly just keep going like that until you get the handling that you're after.
